WEBVTT

00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:35.060
embodies Goryeo's founding principles of restoring Goryeo's territories and

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:40.860
Joseon's spirit of Seonbi. The progress line of Goryeo Pumsae, which

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:45.660
represents the spirit of an upright and strong Seonbi, is the character Sa,

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:52.220
which means Seonbi. We will now take a look at the key moves of Goryeo Pumsae.

00:00:52.220 --> 00:02:09.920
Goryeo Pumsae consists of 13 moves, namely Tongilgi Junbi Jase,

00:02:09.920 --> 00:03:05.700
and Byeojok Jirugi. We will now take a closer look at each of the key moves of Goryeo Pumsae,

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:10.200
Goryopumse begins with Tongmilgi Junbijase.

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:18.100
Open your hands so your palms are face up, then start in front of the lower abdomen,

00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:24.380
past the chest and push forward so your hand blades face forward between the philtrum and neck.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:28.620
The tips of the hands are placed at the philtrum level.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:33.980
Your palms should face each other and maintain a face length between them.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:44.500
The angle of the arms should be 90 to 120 degrees, and your thumbs should be touching your hands.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:52.340
Do not straighten the thumbs. Do not raise the elbows.

00:03:52.340 --> 00:03:57.380
Your elbows should not rise when your hands are raised.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:02.180
The palms of your hands should not be visible when seen from the front.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:12.870
Goryopchagi is a technique used to perform kicks with the same leg two or more times in succession.

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:18.350
You usually strike an opponent's lower body, torso or face in succession.

00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:25.310
Draw the attention of an opponent with the first kick, then dominate them with the second kick

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:33.030
or trip and block against an opponent's attack with the first kick and dominate them with the second kick.

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:46.960
Goryopchagi can be applied with various forms of kicks such as Goryopapchagi, Goryopyopchagi, Goryopdoryochagi, etc.

00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:54.160
Chochojjirugi is a technique used to strike an opponent's lower abdomen downward

00:04:54.160 --> 00:04:59.070
after pulling back the tip of the hand.

00:04:59.070 --> 00:05:06.590
In Goryopumsae, Rullokkeokgi is a technique of using the arc fist, agmuson, downward

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:12.270
and holding an opponent's arm or leg with the other hand to press and twist.

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:16.550
You typically press and twist their joints to dominate them.

00:05:16.550 --> 00:05:23.710
Besides pressing down and twisting the joints, another goal of Goryopumsae is to strike or push an opponent

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:31.320
by pressing, twisting their kneecap, disrupting their balance.

00:05:31.320 --> 00:05:39.360
Palgumchiyopchigi is a technique that uses the edge of the elbow with the fist

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:49.100
and elbow in alignment to attack an opponent in a straight line from the inside out.

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:59.690
Sonnalbakkachigi is a technique that uses a reversed hand blade to attack from the inside out.

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:04.730
The target is an opponent's face and torso.

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:13.740
Sonnalaremakki is the same as aremakki, but it can also be used to strike and block an opponent's attack

00:06:13.740 --> 00:06:20.850
by opening the hand, or used as baramakki and koramakki.

00:06:20.850 --> 00:06:26.650
Agunsonapchigi is a technique typically used to attack an opponent's neck

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:32.200
with the arch of the arc fist and arm placed in a line.

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:39.040
To achieve a hard strike and prevent injuries, the wrist must be properly straightened.

00:06:39.040 --> 00:06:48.540
Your forefingers should be twisted to face outward rather than forward, and your wrist should be straight.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:56.180
Batangsonnulomakki is a technique used to press and block downward.

00:06:56.180 --> 00:07:00.060
The palm of your hand is level with the solar plexus,

00:07:00.060 --> 00:07:06.260
and the space between your arm and torso should be about one fist.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:11.850
The blocking arm should be parallel to the ground.

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:23.370
Mejumokpyojeokarechigi is a technique used to slowly draw a circle with your arms, cross above your head.

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:27.130
Open your right hand in front of the lower abdomen,

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:32.690
then lightly hit your right palm with a left hammer fist.

00:07:32.690 --> 00:07:43.760
The fist should be made at the shoulder line, slowly with a breath.

00:07:43.760 --> 00:07:46.080
Naturally bend your arms.

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:53.670
Be careful not to straighten your wrists when your arms come down drawing a circle.

00:07:53.670 --> 00:08:02.510
Anpalmokhaechomakki is a technique used to block inside out using the inner wrist of your arms.

00:08:02.510 --> 00:08:08.350
The inner wrist should be level with your solar plexus when blocking defending the torso,

00:08:08.350 --> 00:08:12.430
and the distance between the two should remain a shoulder's length.

00:08:12.430 --> 00:08:16.190
Your elbow should face downward without detaching from the body,

00:08:16.190 --> 00:08:22.610
and be careful the move does not resemble Deungjumokapchigi.

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:30.370
Sonnalyeopmakki is a technique to block the sides by performing Sonnalbakkanmakki

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:36.890
by standing sideways like standing in the Juchumseogi posture.

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:43.090
A reminder, the direction of the force progresses inside out.

00:08:43.090 --> 00:08:47.890
The last of the 13 key moves is Pyojeokjirugi.

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:53.090
Pyojeokjirugi is a technique used to create a target with the palm of the hand.

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:57.930
Perform Jirugi toward the palm with the fist.

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:01.490
It is used to connect other techniques by pulling an opponent

00:09:01.490 --> 00:09:07.380
using the force gathered in your hands after the Jirugi.

00:09:07.380 --> 00:09:13.100
It is important to place the target and fist at the solar plexus level.

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:18.460
These are the 13 key moves of Goryeopumse.

00:09:18.500 --> 00:09:24.060
We will now look at the moves in succession connecting each move.

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:35.550
The key moves of Goryeo first part consist of Tongmilgi Jumbijase.

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:39.270
Wen Sonnal Go-du-ro Makki

00:09:39.270 --> 00:09:42.230
Orun Go-dup Yeop-cha-ki

00:09:42.230 --> 00:09:45.350
Orun Sonnal Bakat-chigi

00:09:45.350 --> 00:09:47.990
Wen Jirugi

00:09:47.990 --> 00:09:52.060
Orun Anmakki

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:55.340
Orun Sonnal Go-du-ro Makki

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:58.140
Wen Go-dup Yeop-cha-ki

00:09:58.140 --> 00:10:01.140
Wen Sonnal Bakat-chigi

00:10:01.140 --> 00:10:03.940
Orun Jirugi

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:07.910
And Wen Anmakki

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:11.590
Reclaim your kicking leg after performing Go-dup Yeop-cha-ki.

00:10:11.590 --> 00:10:16.110
Then perform the preparatory Sonnal Bakat-chigi move.

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:23.030
Complete Sonnal Bakat-chigi when the ball and heel of the right foot touch the ground.

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:26.590
The hand blade should be slightly above the shoulder

00:10:26.590 --> 00:10:32.180
and the target of the hand blade is the opponent's neck.

00:10:32.180 --> 00:10:35.180
Push off the ground with the front foot from Jirugi

00:10:35.180 --> 00:10:41.270
and continue with Anmakki by moving your center backwards.

00:10:41.270 --> 00:10:49.540
Change direction using the ball of the leg that acts as the central axis when turning and setting.

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:51.660
Cautions for Goryeo Il-jang

00:10:51.660 --> 00:10:55.450
Taking a closer look

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:59.330
When performing the second Yeop-cha-ki during Go-dup Yeop-cha-ki,

00:10:59.330 --> 00:11:03.810
the heel of the supporting foot should face the direction of the kick.

00:11:03.810 --> 00:11:08.490
The force of the hand blade should be transferred from the inside out.

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:12.050
When turning and setting, be careful not to change direction

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:17.680
using the heel of the leg acting as the central axis.

00:11:17.680 --> 00:11:38.060
We will now practice the moves of Goryeo Il-jang in succession while watching the video.

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:41.860
The key moves of Goryeo second part consist of

00:11:41.860 --> 00:11:44.100
Wen Sonnal Aremakki

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:46.780
Orun Agun Sonap-chigi

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:48.900
Orun Ap-cha-ki

00:11:48.900 --> 00:11:51.860
Orun Sonnal Aremakki

00:11:51.860 --> 00:11:55.180
Wen Agun Sonap-chigi

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:57.820
Wen Ap-cha-ki

00:11:57.820 --> 00:12:00.740
Wen Sonnal Aremakki

00:12:00.740 --> 00:12:03.820
Orun Agun Sonap-chigi

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:06.740
Orun Ap-cha-ki

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:09.100
Wen Nullo Kkeok-ki

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:12.830
Anpalmok Haecho-makki

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:15.750
Wen Ap-cha-ki

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:18.950
Orun Nullo Kkeok-ki

00:12:18.950 --> 00:12:24.050
And Anpalmok Haecho-makki

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:28.530
Sonnal Aremakki is used not only for striking and blocking,

00:12:28.530 --> 00:12:33.450
but also apply to Godomaki and Paramaki.

00:12:33.450 --> 00:12:36.930
It is effective to block an opponent's inner or outer leg

00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:41.880
when striking and blocking an opponent's attack.

00:12:41.880 --> 00:12:49.370
The space between the thigh and the hand should be about two raised fists length.

00:12:49.370 --> 00:12:53.690
Sonnal Aremakki and Agun Sonap-chigi are connected

00:12:53.730 --> 00:12:58.860
and should be performed quickly in succession.

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:03.420
Ap-cha-ki and Sonnal Aremakki should connect without pause.

00:13:03.420 --> 00:13:07.740
You need to control your breath to achieve a harmonious movement.

00:13:07.740 --> 00:13:10.020
When blocking defending the torso,

00:13:10.020 --> 00:13:12.820
your fists should be level with the solar plexus.

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:16.860
Remember that your fists should not rise above your shoulders.

00:13:16.860 --> 00:13:22.980
Also, the left arm crosses outside the right foot if the left foot is in front,

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:29.940
and the right foot crosses outside the left foot if the right foot is in front.

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:34.820
Cautions for Koryo second part, taking a closer look.

00:13:34.820 --> 00:13:42.270
Do not overextend the elbow of the blocking arm during the Sonnal Aremakki move.

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:48.550
Also, be careful not to rely solely on the strength of the arm to block.

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:51.990
During Ap-cha-ki, do not pause before the kick

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:58.640
or fold and raise the leg past the supporting leg to make the kick.

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:06.480
When performing Nullo-koki, the hand should not be above or below the elbow.

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:13.200
Do not use the palm of your hand with the wrist used to press and twist upward.

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:19.280
Concentrate force so that only the narrow part of the arc fist touches the target.

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:25.040
During Anpal-mok Hachomakki, do not cross your fists like Dung-jumok Ap-chigi

00:14:25.040 --> 00:14:27.920
and turn forward on the inside.

00:14:27.920 --> 00:14:33.620
Your center should not be on your hind leg during Ap-sugi.

00:14:33.620 --> 00:14:54.680
We will now practice the moves of Koryo second part in succession while watching the video.

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:58.160
The key moves to Koryo third part consist of

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:01.360
Wen-Sonnal Yeopmakki

00:15:01.360 --> 00:15:04.240
Oren-pyo-jok-ji-ri-ki

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:07.860
Wen-yeop-cha-ki

00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:11.020
Wen-cho-cho-ji-ri-ki

00:15:11.020 --> 00:15:13.660
Oren-are-mak-ki

00:15:13.660 --> 00:15:16.540
Wen-pa-dang-son-neul-o-mak-ki

00:15:16.540 --> 00:15:19.780
Oren-pal-gum-chi-yeop-chigi

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:23.260
Oren-son-nal-yeop-mak-ki

00:15:23.260 --> 00:15:26.300
Wen-pyo-jok-ji-ri-ki

00:15:26.300 --> 00:15:29.620
Oren-yeop-cha-ki

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:33.100
Oren-cho-cho-ji-ri-ki

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:36.300
Wen-are-mak-ki

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:39.420
Oren-pa-dang-son-neul-o-mak-ki

00:15:39.420 --> 00:15:44.100
and Wen-pal-gum-chi-yeop-chigi

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:49.100
Son-nal-yeop-mak-ki is performed by turning and setting the right foot backwards

00:15:49.100 --> 00:15:52.860
using the left ball as the axis from the previous move

00:15:52.860 --> 00:15:56.220
and assuming the Juchum-seogi posture.

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:59.660
Do not forget that the elevation of the thrusting fist

00:15:59.660 --> 00:16:02.620
and the palm of the hand acting as a target

00:16:02.620 --> 00:16:05.940
should be level with the solar plexus.

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:08.940
The thrusting arm should straighten

00:16:08.940 --> 00:16:13.340
and the target arm should straighten naturally.

00:16:13.340 --> 00:16:16.420
The connection of Pyo-jok-ji-ri-ki and Yeop-cha-ki

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:20.780
is repeated twice in Goryeo 3rd part.

00:16:20.780 --> 00:16:25.780
The two arms should remain in place until the Yeop-cha-ki.

00:16:25.780 --> 00:16:27.300
For Pyo-jok-ji-ri-ki,

00:16:27.300 --> 00:16:31.140
imagine an opponent forcefully holding your arm.

00:16:31.140 --> 00:16:34.260
Pull with assistance of the force from the other arm

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:36.780
then connect with a Yeop-cha-ki attack.

00:16:36.780 --> 00:16:40.100
Move and set your right foot in front of your left foot

00:16:40.100 --> 00:16:41.540
with Go-ha-seo-gi.

00:16:41.540 --> 00:16:43.660
Bend and raise your left leg.

00:16:43.700 --> 00:16:46.460
Pull your arms to the right side of your waist.

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:51.260
Then perform Do-jok-ji and Yeop-cha-ki at the same time.

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:53.500
Pulling of the two fists to the back

00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:55.740
and the Yeop-cha-ki move must be balanced

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:59.300
in terms of force and speed.

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:00.900
The heel of the supporting leg

00:17:00.900 --> 00:17:04.500
should point in the direction of the kick.

00:17:04.500 --> 00:17:06.180
The target of the Yeop-cha-ki

00:17:06.180 --> 00:17:09.700
is an opponent's face, torso and lower body

00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:12.020
and can be changed depending on the level

00:17:12.020 --> 00:17:14.860
and the objective of training.

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:16.980
The back of the hand should face upward

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:20.340
at the solar plexus after Yeop-cha-ki.

00:17:20.340 --> 00:17:23.380
Twist the wrist so the palm faces upward.

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:27.220
Then strike the pressure point in the lower abdomen.

00:17:27.220 --> 00:17:30.020
The heel of the foot that performed Yeop-cha-ki

00:17:30.020 --> 00:17:32.300
should touch the ground at the same time

00:17:32.300 --> 00:17:36.580
Jo-jok-ji-ri-ki is performed to finish the move.

00:17:36.580 --> 00:17:38.980
Cautions for Goryeo third part.

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:41.860
Taking a closer look.

00:17:41.860 --> 00:17:43.820
During Son-na Yeop-mak-ki,

00:17:43.820 --> 00:17:45.300
the force from the blocking arm

00:17:45.300 --> 00:17:47.820
should not be directed forward.

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:50.340
The two arms that performed Pyo-jok-ji-ri-ki

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:55.460
must remain in place until Yeop-cha-ki is performed.

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:58.940
Ko-ha-seo-ki posture is assumed before Yeop-cha-ki

00:17:58.940 --> 00:18:02.220
and your fists must not be pulled back.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:04.900
Do not kick above the head with Yeop-cha-ki

00:18:04.900 --> 00:18:09.660
and be careful not to let your head fall below your back.

00:18:09.700 --> 00:18:12.740
We will now practice the moves of Goryeo third part

00:18:12.740 --> 00:18:35.740
in succession while watching the video.

00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:39.260
The key moves of Goryeo fourth part consist of

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:48.420
Me-jumok-pyo-jok-are-chi-gi

00:18:48.420 --> 00:18:51.260
Wen-seon-nal-pak-ga-chi-gi

00:18:51.260 --> 00:18:54.180
Wen-seon-nal-are-mak-gi

00:18:54.180 --> 00:18:57.220
O-reun-seon-nal-an-chi-gi

00:18:57.220 --> 00:19:00.140
O-reun-seon-nal-are-mak-gi

00:19:00.140 --> 00:19:02.540
Wen-seon-nal-an-chi-gi

00:19:02.540 --> 00:19:05.900
Wen-seon-nal-are-mak-gi

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:09.860
and O-reun-ak-um-seon-ap-chi-gi

00:19:09.860 --> 00:19:14.340
In Goryeo fourth part, you can attack upward and block downward

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:18.620
with Seon-nal-chi-gi and Seon-nal-are-mak-gi in succession,

00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:25.460
but it is also possible to attack by quickly applying the upward and downward move.

00:19:25.460 --> 00:19:28.140
The lower body should hold steady.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:35.720
The torso should be flexible through your central axis with appropriate breathing.

00:19:35.720 --> 00:19:38.120
Cautions for Goryeo fourth part.

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:41.320
Taking a closer look.

00:19:41.320 --> 00:19:43.520
When performing Seon-nal-an-chi-gi,

00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:49.320
the elbow should not move forward and assume a Seon-kut-jir-gi posture.

00:19:49.320 --> 00:19:56.280
The elbow of the blocking arm should not overextend when performing Seon-nal-are-mak-gi.

00:19:56.280 --> 00:20:22.730
We will now practice the moves of Goryeo fourth part in succession while watching the video.

00:20:22.730 --> 00:20:27.010
You are now on the verge of becoming a master of Goryeo pumsae.

00:20:27.010 --> 00:21:37.110
We will take another look at all the moves and master pumsae.

00:21:37.110 --> 00:21:40.030
We have looked at the key moves of Goryeo pumsae

00:21:40.030 --> 00:21:45.390
and provided thorough explanations for each move and things to watch out for.

00:21:45.390 --> 00:21:49.150
You will be able to master much better postures and techniques

00:21:49.150 --> 00:21:54.390
by training the Goryeo pumsae and reminding yourself of the spirit of Seon-bi.

00:21:54.390 --> 00:21:57.830
We will see you again in the Geumgang pumsae video.

00:21:57.830 --> 00:21:59.030
Thanks for watching.

